ready asked and got no observations. So we lack evidence. Might need to ask about Candidate A's crew cooperation? Or about Candidate B's reliability? But we have some.\n\nWe could propose focusing on crew cooperation and professional communication for all candidates, as it's critical. But we already asked about D and C; maybe ask about A and B? However we have some private notes: A show-off, not open to new ideas (cooperation maybe). B makes nasty remarks (cooperation). So we have some.\n\nThus we can give provisional recommendation: Candidate A seems strongest technically but concerns on openness and teamwork. Candidate B good stress and conscientious but communication issues. Candidate C good calm and decision but egocentric. Candidate D strong problem solving and responsibility but hot temper.\n\nProbably the best overall might be Candidate A if we can mitigate openness, but the hot temper of D may be more severe. I'd propose provisional vote for Candidate A, but note concerns about teamwork and openness, and suggest we need more evidence on crew cooperation for all.\n\nThus contribution: share private observations for each candidate, compare on key criteria, give provisional vote for A, and highlight need to discuss crew cooperation and communication.\n\nLet's craft public message: brief.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate A."}
